# @!method self.call(user, actor, pipeline, stages)
#   Soft-deletes the given stages of a live pipeline together with their jobs and hands
#   physical destruction to the async pipeline destroy workflow, scoped to those stages.
#   The subtree is only marked deleted here: both Pipeline::Stage and Pipeline::StageClient
#   default-scope deleted rows away, so the stages disappear from the app the moment this
#   commits, while the physical delete — thousands of cascading DELETEs — is reaped by the
#   workflow in chunked background transactions. Inline it outlives the DB lock/statement
#   timeouts on a large stage and kills the request.
def initialize(user, actor, pipeline, stages)
  @user = user
  @actor = actor
  @pipeline = pipeline
  @stages = stages
  @firm = user.firm
end

